IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`

-- Tests for au-interpretation-time.l4. EVERY expected value is written by hand from
-- the text (the section and example are named beside it), and weekdays were taken
-- from a calendar, not from the encoding. A failing assertion is a finding.

`no closures` MEANS `Days of closure` OF EMPTY, EMPTY

§ `Section 2B: business day, calendar month, calendar year, financial year`

-- 2026-02-02 is a Monday, 2026-01-31 a Saturday, 2026-02-01 a Sunday.
#ASSERT `is a business day` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 2) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT (`is a business day` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a business day` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) EMPTY)
-- A Monday that is a public holiday in the place is not a business day.
#ASSERT NOT (`is a business day` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) (LIST YearMonthDay 2026 6 1))
#ASSERT `is a business day` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 2) (LIST YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)
-- "calendar month means one of the 12 months of the year".
#ASSERT `is one of the 12 calendar months` 1
#ASSERT `is one of the 12 calendar months` 12
#ASSERT NOT (`is one of the 12 calendar months` 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`is one of the 12 calendar months` 13)
#ASSERT NOT (`is one of the 12 calendar months` 1.5)
-- "calendar year means a period of 12 months starting on 1 January".
#ASSERT `the calendar year containing` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) EQUALS `A span of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2026 12 31)
-- "financial year means a period of 12 months starting on 1 July".
#ASSERT `the financial year containing` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 15) EQUALS `A span of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1), (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT `the financial year containing` (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) EQUALS `A span of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1), (YearMonthDay 2027 6 30)
#ASSERT `the financial year containing` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) EQUALS `A span of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1), (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)

§ `Section 2G: months (the four printed examples, then the edges)`

-- 2G(1) example 1: a month starting on 15 December ends immediately before 15 January.
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 15) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 1 14
-- 2G(1) example 2: a month starting on 31 August ends at the end of September.
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 9 30
-- 2G(2) example 1: 6 months starting on 15 December end immediately before 15 June.
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `calendar months starting on` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 15) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 6 14
-- 2G(2) example 2: 6 months starting on 31 October end at the end of April.
#ASSERT `the last day of` 6 `calendar months starting on` (YearMonthDay 2025 10 31) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 30
-- A month starting on the 1st ends on the last day of the same month.
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 3 31
-- 29, 30 and 31 January: no corresponding day in a short February.
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 29) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 30) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 31) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 2 28
-- In a leap year 29 February exists: a month starting on 29 January ends immediately before it.
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 29) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2024 2 28
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 30) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2024 2 29
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 31) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2024 2 29
-- Across the end of a year.
#ASSERT `the last day of` 12 `calendar months starting on` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 12 31
#ASSERT `the last day of` 13 `calendar months starting on` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 15) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2027 1 14
#ASSERT `the last day of` 2 `calendar months starting on` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 31) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 28
-- Starting on a leap day: 12 months end at the end of February 2025; 48 months end
-- immediately before 29 February 2028.
#ASSERT `the last day of` 12 `calendar months starting on` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `the last day of` 48 `calendar months starting on` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2028 2 28

§ `Section 36(1): the table of seven items`

-- Items 1 to 4 include the specified day; items 5 to 7 do not.
#ASSERT `a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` `between two days`
#ASSERT `a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` `begins at, on or with a specified day`
#ASSERT `a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` `continues until a specified day`
#ASSERT `a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` `ends at, on or with a specified day`
#ASSERT NOT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` `begins from a specified day`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` `begins after a specified day`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` `ends before a specified day`)
-- Example 1: between 1 September and 30 November, both days count.
#ASSERT `the first day of the period` `between two days` (YearMonthDay 2026 9 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 9 1)
#ASSERT `the last day of the period` `between two days` (YearMonthDay 2026 11 30) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 11 30)
-- Example 2: a permission that begins on the first day of a financial year is in force on that day.
#ASSERT `the first day of the period` `begins at, on or with a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1)
-- Example 3: a licence that continues until 31 March is valid up to and including 31 March.
#ASSERT `the last day of the period` `continues until a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31)
-- Example 4: a right that ends on the last day of a financial year may be exercised on that day.
#ASSERT `the last day of the period` `ends at, on or with a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30)
-- Example 5: expressed to operate from 30 June, it starts to operate on 1 July.
#ASSERT `the first day of the period` `begins from a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1)
-- Example 6: a decision made on 2 August and 28 days after the day it is made: the period begins on 3 August.
#ASSERT `the first day of the period` `begins after a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2026 8 2) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 8 3)
-- Example 7: the 7 days before the day a proceeding starts on 8 May run from 1 May to 7 May.
#ASSERT `the last day of the period` `ends before a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 8) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 7)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 7 Days `starting on` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 7)
-- A start expression gives no last day, and an end expression gives no first day.
#ASSERT `the last day of the period` `begins from a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the first day of the period` `ends before a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 8) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Lengths: days, months, and what the text does not say (weeks, years)`

-- A period of 1 day starting on a day is that day; 28 days starting 3 August end on 30 August (examples 6 and 7).
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 Days `starting on` (YearMonthDay 2026 8 3) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 8 3)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 28 Days `starting on` (YearMonthDay 2026 8 3) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 8 30)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 Months `starting on` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 14)
-- Weeks and years: the Act does not give their length (it never uses the word week).
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 2 Weeks `starting on` (YearMonthDay 2026 8 3) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 Years `starting on` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 17) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A length that is not a whole number of at least 1 has no last day.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 0 Days `starting on` (YearMonthDay 2026 8 3) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` (0 MINUS 5) Months `starting on` (YearMonthDay 2026 8 3) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1.5 Days `starting on` (YearMonthDay 2026 8 3) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `The worked cases (NOTES.md answer table)`

-- W1 three years from 2025-07-16: the first day is 2025-07-17 (item 5); the Act gives no length for a year.
#ASSERT `the first day of the period` `begins from a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 16) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 7 17)
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 3 Years `that` `begins from a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 16) EQUALS NOTHING
-- ... on the ALTERNATIVE reading (a year is 12 months): 36 months from 2025-07-17 end immediately before 2028-07-17.
#ASSERT `ALTERNATIVE READING: the last day of a counted period, expressed as` `begins from a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 16) 3 Years EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2028 7 16)
-- W2 five years from 2025-01-15 and from 2025-09-01 (alternative reading).
#ASSERT `ALTERNATIVE READING: the last day of a counted period, expressed as` `begins from a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) 5 Years EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2030 1 15)
#ASSERT `ALTERNATIVE READING: the last day of a counted period, expressed as` `begins from a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) 5 Years EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2030 9 1)
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 5 Years `that` `begins from a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) EQUALS NOTHING
-- W3 thirty days from 2026-01-01: the first day is 2026-01-02 and the last day 2026-01-31, a Saturday.
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 30 Days `that` `begins from a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31)
-- ... which s 36(2) moves to Monday 2026-02-02 (Sunday 1 February is also a rest day).
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) `no closures` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 2
-- ... and to Tuesday 3 February if Monday 2 February is a public holiday.
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) (`Days of closure` OF (LIST YearMonthDay 2026 2 2), EMPTY) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 3
-- W4 two years from 2024-02-28: the first day is 2024-02-29; alternative reading: 24 months, no 29 February in 2026.
#ASSERT `the first day of the period` `begins from a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 28) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29)
#ASSERT `ALTERNATIVE READING: the last day of a counted period, expressed as` `begins from a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 28) 2 Years EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 2 Years `that` `begins from a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 28) EQUALS NOTHING
-- ... 2026-02-28 is a Saturday: s 36(2) moves it to Monday 2026-03-02.
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28) `no closures` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 2
-- W5 one year from 2024-02-29: the first day is 2024-03-01; alternative reading: 12 months end immediately before 1 March 2025.
#ASSERT `ALTERNATIVE READING: the last day of a counted period, expressed as` `begins from a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29) 1 Years EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 2 28)
-- W6 one month from 2025-01-31: the first day is 2025-02-01; the month ends immediately before 1 March: 2025-02-28.
#ASSERT `the first day of the period` `begins from a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 31) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 2 1)
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 1 Months `that` `begins from a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 31) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 2 28)
-- 2025-02-28 is a Friday: no s 36(2) move.
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 2 28) `no closures` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 2 28

§ `Fork F1: does "one month from 15 December" count 15 December? (item 5 says it does not)`

-- 2G alone ("a month starting on 15 December") ends on 14 January; item 5 composed with 2G
-- ("one month from 15 December") begins on 16 December and ends on 15 January.
#ASSERT `the last day of a month starting on` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 15) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 1 14
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 1 Months `that` `begins from a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 1 Months `that` `begins at, on or with a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 14)
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 1 Months `that` `begins after a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15)

§ `Fork F3: s 36(2) reaches a last day counted in months or years as well as in days`

-- One month from 2026-01-31 ends on Saturday 2026-02-28; the thing may be done on Monday 2026-03-02.
#ASSERT `the last day of a counted period of` 1 Months `that` `begins from a specified day` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28) `no closures` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 2

§ `Section 36(2) and (3)`

-- The text's own example: 31 March is a Saturday (2018), so the thing may be done on Monday 2 April.
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2018 3 31) `no closures` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2018 4 2
-- A weekday last day does not move.
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 2 2) `no closures` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 2
-- Limb (a) not met (no Act requires or allows the thing): the rule does not move the day.
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2018 3 31) `no closures` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2018 3 31
-- Several days in a row: Friday 2026-04-03 and Monday 2026-04-06 are holidays; Saturday and Sunday between: the next day is Tuesday 7 April.
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 3) (`Days of closure` OF (LIST YearMonthDay 2026 4 3, YearMonthDay 2026 4 6), EMPTY) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 7
-- If the office is also closed for the whole of Tuesday 7 April, the next day is Wednesday 8 April.
#ASSERT `the last day on which the thing may be done` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 3) (`Days of closure` OF (LIST YearMonthDay 2026 4 3, YearMonthDay 2026 4 6), (LIST YearMonthDay 2026 4 7)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 4 8
-- Holiday means (a) a public holiday in the place AND (b) a day the office is closed for the whole day: either is a holiday.
#ASSERT `is a holiday for the time for doing a thing` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 7) (`Days of closure` OF EMPTY, (LIST YearMonthDay 2026 4 7))
#ASSERT `is a holiday for the time for doing a thing` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 7) (`Days of closure` OF (LIST YearMonthDay 2026 4 7), EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a holiday for the time for doing a thing` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 8) (`Days of closure` OF (LIST YearMonthDay 2026 4 7), (LIST YearMonthDay 2026 4 7)))
-- The business-day definition (2B) knows only public holidays, not office closures.
#ASSERT `is a business day` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 7) EMPTY
-- Within the time allowed: the period begins 2026-01-02 and its last day 2026-01-31 is a Saturday.
#ASSERT `the thing is done within the time allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) `no closures`
#ASSERT `the thing is done within the time allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) `no closures`
#ASSERT `the thing is done within the time allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) `no closures`
#ASSERT NOT (`the thing is done within the time allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 3) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) `no closures`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the thing is done within the time allowed` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 2) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) `no closures`)
-- Days of rest INSIDE a period still count towards its length (nothing in the text excludes them): 30 days from 2026-01-01 still end on 2026-01-31 though 3 and 4, 10 and 11, ... are weekends.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 30 Days `starting on` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 2) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31)

§ `Part 3: when an Act comes into operation (ss 3 and 3A)`

-- W7 an Act assented to on 2026-03-10 that says nothing: the 28th day after is 2026-04-07 (3A(2)), at the start of the day (s 3).
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `Act` `silent about commencement` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 7)
#ASSERT `the moment the enactment comes into operation` `Act` `silent about commencement` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST (`Moment in a day` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 4 7), 0, 0, 0)
-- Month-end arithmetic on the 28 days.
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `Act` `silent about commencement` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `Act` `silent about commencement` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29)
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `Act` `silent about commencement` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 7)
-- 3A(3): an Act to alter the Constitution commences on the day of Royal Assent.
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `Act to alter the Constitution` `silent about commencement` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10)
-- 3A(1): an Act that provides for its own commencement is not given the 28 days.
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `Act` (`commencement on a particular day` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)
-- W8 a day to be fixed later: until it is fixed, no day; once fixed as 2026-06-01, the start of that day (s 3).
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `Act` `commencement on a day still to be fixed` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the moment the enactment comes into operation` `Act` `commencement on a day still to be fixed` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the moment the enactment comes into operation` `Act` (`commencement on a day fixed later` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST (`Moment in a day` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1), 0, 0, 0)
-- W9 subordinate legislation made on 2026-03-10 that says nothing: the text gives no default.
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `legislative instrument` `silent about commencement` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `notifiable instrument` `silent about commencement` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day the enactment commences` `other instrument made under a power` `silent about commencement` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the moment the enactment comes into operation` `legislative instrument` `silent about commencement` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS NOTHING
-- An instrument that names a day does come into operation at the start of it.
#ASSERT `the moment the enactment comes into operation` `legislative instrument` (`commencement on a particular day` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1)) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) EQUALS JUST (`Moment in a day` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1), 0, 0, 0)

§ `Part 6: service by post (s 29)`

-- Properly addressed, prepaid, posted as a letter: taken to be effected on the day the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post.
#ASSERT `the day service by post is taken to be effected` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 14) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 14)
-- Unless the contrary is proved.
#ASSERT `the day service by post is taken to be effected` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 14) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20)
-- Each of the three conditions is needed.
#ASSERT `the day service by post is taken to be effected` FALSE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 14) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day service by post is taken to be effected` TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 14) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day service by post is taken to be effected` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 3 14) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 37A: attaining an age`

-- Born 17 May 2000: attains 18 at the start of 17 May 2018.
#ASSERT `the moment a person attains the age` (YearMonthDay 2000 5 17) 18 EQUALS JUST (`Moment in a day` OF (YearMonthDay 2018 5 17), 0, 0, 0)
-- Born 29 February 2000: the 4th and 24th anniversaries fall on leap days; the 1st does not exist.
#ASSERT `the moment a person attains the age` (YearMonthDay 2000 2 29) 4 EQUALS JUST (`Moment in a day` OF (YearMonthDay 2004 2 29), 0, 0, 0)
#ASSERT `the moment a person attains the age` (YearMonthDay 2000 2 29) 24 EQUALS JUST (`Moment in a day` OF (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29), 0, 0, 0)
#ASSERT `the moment a person attains the age` (YearMonthDay 2000 2 29) 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the moment a person attains the age` (YearMonthDay 2000 2 29) 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the moment a person attains the age` (YearMonthDay 2000 5 17) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the moment a person attains the age` (YearMonthDay 2000 5 17) 2.5 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 2M: sitting day`

`the Senate sits Thursday into Friday` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 6)
`the House sits Wednesday into Thursday` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5)
`the House sits again on Thursday` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5)

-- Example 1: the Senate begins sitting on Thursday 2026-03-05 and is adjourned on Friday 2026-03-06: Thursday is a sitting day, Friday is not.
#ASSERT `is a sitting day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) (LIST `the Senate sits Thursday into Friday`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a sitting day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 6) (LIST `the Senate sits Thursday into Friday`))
-- Example 2: Wednesday 2026-03-04 into Thursday, then a second sitting on Thursday: both are sitting days.
#ASSERT `is a sitting day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4) (LIST `the House sits Wednesday into Thursday`, `the House sits again on Thursday`)
#ASSERT `is a sitting day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) (LIST `the House sits Wednesday into Thursday`, `the House sits again on Thursday`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a sitting day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 6) (LIST `the House sits Wednesday into Thursday`, `the House sits again on Thursday`))
-- Without the second sitting Thursday is only part of Wednesday's sitting day.
#ASSERT NOT (`is a sitting day` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) (LIST `the House sits Wednesday into Thursday`))

`a sitting on 3 March` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 3), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 3)
`a sitting on 4 March` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4)
`a sitting on 10 March` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10)
`a second sitting on 10 March` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10)
`a sitting on 11 March` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11)
`a sitting on 12 March` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 12), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 12)
`a sitting on 17 March` MEANS `A sitting of a House` OF (YearMonthDay 2026 3 17), (YearMonthDay 2026 3 17)

`some sittings` MEANS LIST `a sitting on 3 March`, `a sitting on 4 March`, `a sitting on 10 March`, `a second sitting on 10 March`, `a sitting on 11 March`, `a sitting on 12 March`, `a sitting on 17 March`

-- The n-th sitting day after a day (strictly after: s 36(1) item 6). After 4 March the sitting days are 10, 11, 12 and 17 March.
#ASSERT `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 1 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4) `some sittings` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 3 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4) `some sittings` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 12)
#ASSERT `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 4 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4) `some sittings` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 17)
#ASSERT `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 5 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4) `some sittings` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 0 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4) `some sittings` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Two sittings that begin on 10 March are one sitting day: the 2nd sitting day after 9 March is 11 March.
#ASSERT `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 2 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9) `some sittings` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11)
-- Strictly after: the 1st sitting day after 10 March is 11 March.
#ASSERT `the sitting day that is the n-th after` 1 (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) `some sittings` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 11)
